1
00:00:01,181 --> 00:00:09,221
The Princess Sapphire
Knight of the Ribbon

2
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,160
♪ Atashi no miru yume himitsu nano ♪
The dreams I see are my secret

3
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:57,089
♪ Dare ni mo iwanai himitsu nano ♪
I won’t tell anyone—it’s my secret

4
00:00:58,541 --> 00:01:02,461
♪ Akai manto hira hira ♪
A red cape fluttering

5
00:01:02,462 --> 00:01:04,981
♪ Uma o tobasu oujo ♪
Galloping on a horse—the princess

6
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,901
♪ Sore ga atashi ♪
That’s me!

7
00:01:07,621 --> 00:01:10,901
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

8
00:01:10,905 --> 00:01:13,424
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

9
00:01:14,541 --> 00:01:18,021
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

10
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:20,741
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

11
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:25,220
♪ Ribon no kishi wa ♪
The Knight of the Ribbon,

12
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:28,621
♪ Honto wa hontto wa ♪
Truly, truly,

13
00:01:28,622 --> 00:01:31,822
♪ Atashi nano sa ♪
It’s really me!

14
00:01:44,101 --> 00:01:50,141
Twenty-First Episode
The Magic Cookies
The World's Best Snack

15
00:02:03,959 --> 00:02:06,726
All right, it's time to wake Lord Sapphire.

16
00:02:08,330 --> 00:02:11,700
Lord Sapphire, it is time.

17
00:02:21,930 --> 00:02:24,980
Lord Sapphire, it's time to go to the secret room.

18
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:26,760
Yeah, I know.

19
00:02:34,010 --> 00:02:35,160
I'll be right back.

20
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:36,973
You must not.

21
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:39,299
Please study properly until nine o'clock.

22
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:56,900
You're late today.

23
00:02:57,024 --> 00:02:58,640
Now, hurry and change.

24
00:02:58,804 --> 00:03:00,520
Allow me to help you.

25
00:03:00,674 --> 00:03:02,000
Here is your dress.

26
00:03:03,260 --> 00:03:04,260
Is this it?

27
00:03:04,386 --> 00:03:06,486
The one Mother made for me?

28
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:08,306
Yes, it is.

29
00:03:08,454 --> 00:03:12,780
You must study cooking and sewing so you won't be outdone by any queen.

30
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:18,260
But if I wear women's clothes, I can't ride my horse!

31
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:21,620
If you act like a proper girl, I'm sure you'll grow to like it.

32
00:03:21,984 --> 00:03:23,258
Come on now, please change.

33
00:03:23,282 --> 00:03:25,260
 I told you, I'll do it myself!

34
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:26,600
Stop nagging me!

35
00:03:31,780 --> 00:03:32,500
Come now.

36
00:03:32,775 --> 00:03:34,259
My, how adorable!

37
00:03:34,495 --> 00:03:36,120
Now first, slice this bread.

38
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:36,520
Okay.

39
00:03:36,964 --> 00:03:38,325
Huh? It won't cut.

40
00:03:38,349 --> 00:03:41,633
When that happens, warming the knife helps it cut easily.

41
00:03:41,658 --> 00:03:42,940
Look, like this.

42
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:46,140
Slice, slice, chop...

43
00:03:52,620 --> 00:03:53,620
This isn't working.

44
00:03:53,780 --> 00:03:54,800
It won't cut right.

45
00:03:55,964 --> 00:03:57,766
Hey, do you have a longer knife?

46
00:03:58,020 --> 00:03:59,666
We have something like this, but...

47
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:02,460
Yeah, this will do.

48
00:04:02,646 --> 00:04:04,864
That's used for preparing fish.

49
00:04:07,426 --> 00:04:08,600
What are you doing?

50
00:04:09,060 --> 00:04:10,060
There! Here we go!

51
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:12,946
Slice, slice, slice, slice!

52
00:04:13,890 --> 00:04:16,277
Wow, this cuts way better!

53
00:04:16,301 --> 00:04:20,420
Ah, no, you can't! When you cook, you have to follow proper cooking rules!

54
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:21,313
Okay.

55
00:04:21,716 --> 00:04:24,240
Good morning, everyone. Oh my...

56
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:26,279
Good morning.

57
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:27,780
You certainly slept in late.

58
00:04:28,260 --> 00:04:30,060
Who is that girl?

59
00:04:32,735 --> 00:04:34,900
Why, if it isn't Sapphire!

60
00:04:36,470 --> 00:04:38,086
Here's breakfast!

61
00:04:38,690 --> 00:04:40,280
Well, isn't that thoughtful of you?

62
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:41,760
Here you go, Father.

63
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:43,160
And this is for Mother.

64
00:04:43,350 --> 00:04:46,146
Hmm, when she acts like this, she really is a girl after all.

65
00:04:46,630 --> 00:04:48,566
See? I can do it if I try.

66
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:53,000
Huh? What's wrong? Why'd you make that weird sound?

67
00:04:53,466 --> 00:04:55,240
Oh, nothing, it's just...

68
00:04:56,115 --> 00:04:57,539
What a sight...

69
00:04:57,665 --> 00:04:59,187
And after I took the trouble to set it so nicely!

70
00:04:59,211 --> 00:05:00,380
Oh, I'm so sorry.

71
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:02,493
Could someone put a tablecloth over it?

72
00:05:02,995 --> 00:05:03,995
Oh, uh, this...

73
00:05:06,070 --> 00:05:07,466
I'm sorry, Father.

74
00:05:08,020 --> 00:05:10,380
Never mind that, just hurry up, Sapphire.

75
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:12,100
Hey, wait a minute.

76
00:05:16,170 --> 00:05:19,020
You really do seem better off as a boy.

77
00:05:24,970 --> 00:05:26,280
What? Nothing at all?

78
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:27,480
Well, actually...

79
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Is that true?

80
00:05:30,716 --> 00:05:31,980
It's these biscuits.

81
00:05:33,235 --> 00:05:33,995
Handstand!

82
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:35,920
Flip!

83
00:05:36,413 --> 00:05:37,413
Bark!

84
00:05:38,970 --> 00:05:41,738
I put a new potion I made into these biscuits—

85
00:05:41,762 --> 00:05:44,220
one that makes people do whatever they're told.

86
00:05:44,395 --> 00:05:46,920
Good. Have them make plenty of those biscuits.

87
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:52,140
And I'll feed it to the King, Queen, and Sapphire at snack time today.

88
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:56,773
That was delicious.

89
00:05:57,355 --> 00:05:59,726
Hey, why did you eat my precious biscuit?

90
00:06:00,905 --> 00:06:02,520
Biscuits that make you do as you're told.

91
00:06:04,756 --> 00:06:07,066
Hey, where are you going, you parrot? Wait!

92
00:06:09,050 --> 00:06:10,880
It's time to become a boy.

93
00:06:11,015 --> 00:06:13,060
It's finally time.

94
00:06:13,455 --> 00:06:15,353
All right, off I go!

95
00:06:16,115 --> 00:06:18,740
Goodness, perhaps I raised her too much like a boy.

96
00:06:19,405 --> 00:06:20,640
What am I going to do with her?

97
00:06:26,180 --> 00:06:27,180
Stop!

98
00:06:29,470 --> 00:06:30,470
It's a parrot.

99
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:31,840
How strange.

100
00:06:31,945 --> 00:06:32,945
Here, perch on my hand.

101
00:06:33,970 --> 00:06:35,560
This is Nylon's pet parrot.

102
00:06:35,660 --> 00:06:36,660
Hey, parrot!

103
00:06:36,700 --> 00:06:38,033
Hey, parrot!

104
00:06:39,610 --> 00:06:40,676
Prince Sapphire!

105
00:06:40,750 --> 00:06:42,053
Nylon, this is yours, right?

106
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:42,780
Here you go.

107
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:45,326
N-No, that won't be necessary.

108
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:47,360
Let's go for a ride later.

109
00:06:48,780 --> 00:06:50,173
That's odd.

110
00:06:50,670 --> 00:06:52,220
I wonder what's wrong with this parrot.

111
00:06:53,420 --> 00:06:55,600
Hey, if you know something, tell me.

112
00:06:56,280 --> 00:06:57,700
Eat a biscuit.

113
00:06:57,960 --> 00:06:58,586
If you eat it?

114
00:06:58,611 --> 00:07:00,480
Make biscuits.

115
00:07:00,905 --> 00:07:02,540
Make biscuits?

116
00:07:02,573 --> 00:07:04,113
Hey, what kind of biscuits?

117
00:07:09,525 --> 00:07:10,525
Duralumin!

118
00:07:10,748 --> 00:07:14,806
This parrot was talking about biscuits laced with an obedience drug!

119
00:07:16,750 --> 00:07:21,120
Biscuits laced with an obedience drug? What on earth is that?

120
00:07:21,380 --> 00:07:22,900
Nylon, do you know something about this?

121
00:07:23,620 --> 00:07:26,043
I have no idea what you mean. I'm completely...

122
00:07:26,687 --> 00:07:27,541
That's a lie!

123
00:07:28,030 --> 00:07:29,366
You looked like you knew a moment ago!

124
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:34,300
What on earth is wrong with you?

125
00:07:34,325 --> 00:07:36,560
You must have had a terrible dream last night.

126
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:44,600
<i>Those biscuits are definitely for some evil plot.</i>

127
00:07:47,230 --> 00:07:49,860
<i>If they're biscuits, they must be having a sweet shop make them.</i>

128
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:52,763
<i>All right, I'm definitely going to find them.</i>

129
00:07:58,507 --> 00:07:59,741
You're Prince Sapphire, right?

130
00:08:00,640 --> 00:08:01,920
Where are you going?

131
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:05,488
There's a pastry shop in the woods! I'm going to go look for it!

132
00:08:34,299 --> 00:08:39,520
This is all sponge cake! The snow on the roof is whipped cream.

133
00:08:41,700 --> 00:08:42,700
How cute.

134
00:08:44,259 --> 00:08:46,899
The popcorn gravel sure is delicious.

135
00:08:47,139 --> 00:08:48,566
Wow, it's tasty!

136
00:08:52,573 --> 00:08:53,573
Hey!

137
00:08:55,620 --> 00:08:57,646
What do you want here?!

138
00:08:59,855 --> 00:09:03,060
Kids who just come to gawk and eat should go home!

139
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:06,060
I'm busy making a huge biscuit order!

140
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:09,220
The biscuit order...

141
00:09:09,979 --> 00:09:11,360
So he really is making them here.

142
00:09:12,180 --> 00:09:13,180
What should I do?

143
00:09:14,520 --> 00:09:14,946
Ah, I know!

144
00:09:15,146 --> 00:09:15,586
Opal!

145
00:09:15,785 --> 00:09:18,026
Go to the castle and fetch me a girl's dress!

146
00:09:23,529 --> 00:09:24,529
Great, this will do.

147
00:09:24,745 --> 00:09:26,560
Now Opal, wait here!

148
00:09:35,270 --> 00:09:36,880
Who is it, when I'm so busy?!

149
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:38,740
Oh, a customer?

150
00:09:40,039 --> 00:09:42,260
No, I'm looking for work.

151
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:47,520
I heard the baker here is a kind person who would surely hire me.

152
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,900
Um, do you have any work for me?

153
00:09:50,759 --> 00:09:53,780
Well, I'm slammed today, so you're hired!

154
00:09:54,195 --> 00:09:55,439
Yay! I'm so happy!

155
00:09:56,750 --> 00:09:59,553
Wait, do you make sweets in a small space like this?

156
00:09:59,610 --> 00:10:00,610
Don't be foolish!

157
00:10:00,675 --> 00:10:03,320
How could I bake cakes in a shop like this?!

158
00:10:05,740 --> 00:10:08,233
Wow, you have a room in the basement too!

159
00:10:21,335 --> 00:10:22,813
What an amazing workshop!

160
00:10:22,870 --> 00:10:23,923
It's magnificent!

161
00:10:24,160 --> 00:10:27,140
After all, I'm the greatest baker in the world!

162
00:10:30,680 --> 00:10:31,680
Sapphire!

163
00:10:31,900 --> 00:10:32,900
Yes!

164
00:10:33,130 --> 00:10:35,400
Light the fire in the furthest stove!

165
00:10:35,900 --> 00:10:36,593
Okay!

166
00:10:37,675 --> 00:10:40,520
Just set it on fire? That's easy!

167
00:10:45,789 --> 00:10:49,280
Well, well, Sapphire. Don't you even know how to start a fire?

168
00:10:49,629 --> 00:10:51,738
I'm sorry, the wood is damp...

169
00:10:51,762 --> 00:10:52,700
Sapphire, look!

170
00:10:52,780 --> 00:10:54,040
Everything's pitch black!

171
00:10:54,460 --> 00:10:56,333
Even the biscuit ingredients are pitch black!

172
00:10:57,255 --> 00:10:59,806
So you won't make any more biscuits?

173
00:10:59,985 --> 00:11:00,835
Don't be ridiculous!

174
00:11:00,860 --> 00:11:02,640
I'll finish it by snack time today!

175
00:11:02,705 --> 00:11:03,705
Clean up!

176
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:04,800
Yes!

177
00:11:19,375 --> 00:11:23,280
Alright. Now to add the medicine they ordered...

178
00:11:30,779 --> 00:11:32,520
Now, you're going to help me.

179
00:11:32,770 --> 00:11:34,998
First, you quickly take the dough,

180
00:11:35,022 --> 00:11:37,040
pat it down like this, and make it about this size.

181
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:39,040
Then you bake it later.

182
00:11:40,275 --> 00:11:42,953
Pat, pat... Huh?

183
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:44,120
It's huge!

184
00:11:53,669 --> 00:11:54,560
Oh, no!

185
00:11:54,690 --> 00:11:55,880
Mine fell apart!

186
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:59,800
Enough! Put the ones I made into the oven!

187
00:12:00,740 --> 00:12:01,740
Okay!

188
00:12:02,620 --> 00:12:02,940
I know!

189
00:12:03,520 --> 00:12:06,220
I'll mess up on purpose and ruin these biscuits!

190
00:12:07,709 --> 00:12:08,709
You fool!

191
00:12:08,780 --> 00:12:10,666
How could you be so careless?!

192
00:12:10,889 --> 00:12:12,180
I'm sorry, Mr. Cookie!

193
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:13,536
I'm so clumsy...

194
00:12:13,560 --> 00:12:16,540
Why can't you handle such a simple task?

195
00:12:16,610 --> 00:12:18,660
Even a baby could do this!

196
00:12:18,661 --> 00:12:20,440
Can't you act like a proper girl?

197
00:12:20,465 --> 00:12:21,700
Old man, you in here?

198
00:12:23,340 --> 00:12:24,340
Old man!

199
00:12:24,539 --> 00:12:25,680
Is our order ready?

200
00:12:25,760 --> 00:12:26,860
I'm baking them right now!

201
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:28,440
You'll have to wait a little longer!

202
00:12:29,430 --> 00:12:30,520
Who's that girl?

203
00:12:31,639 --> 00:12:32,840
She's my assistant.

204
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:34,000
Right, fresh out of the oven!

205
00:12:34,130 --> 00:12:35,130
Help me out!

206
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:36,413
Yes!

207
00:12:37,430 --> 00:12:38,040
Very good!

208
00:12:38,325 --> 00:12:39,780
We'll take the cookies!

209
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:43,660
By the way, what medicine did you put in these sweets?

210
00:12:44,085 --> 00:12:45,719
It isn't poison, is it?

211
00:12:45,779 --> 00:12:46,779
Don't be ridiculous!

212
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:48,660
It's a supplement called Vitamin C!

213
00:12:49,119 --> 00:12:50,840
A supplement... <i>Could it be</i>...?

214
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:52,920
Girl!

215
00:12:53,069 --> 00:12:54,660
Why did you just say "could it be"?

216
00:12:54,775 --> 00:12:57,186
You know something about these biscuits, don't you?

217
00:12:57,259 --> 00:12:58,666
N-N-No, I don't know a thing!

218
00:12:58,740 --> 00:13:00,493
Nothing about any medicine...

219
00:13:02,900 --> 00:13:05,266
These are just delicious biscuits!

220
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:08,700
Is that so?

221
00:13:09,020 --> 00:13:11,680
Then you can eat one of these biscuits!

222
00:13:11,820 --> 00:13:14,000
They're just biscuits with Vitamin C, right?

223
00:13:14,385 --> 00:13:15,385
Go on, try it!

224
00:13:15,680 --> 00:13:16,680
Eat it!

225
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:18,240
Come on, eat up!

226
00:13:25,919 --> 00:13:26,919
Go on, eat!

227
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:28,320
Try a bite!

228
00:13:32,609 --> 00:13:33,960
All right!

229
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:34,680
It's true!

230
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:36,680
She knows about the biscuits!

231
00:13:36,920 --> 00:13:37,920
Was it bitter?

232
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:39,120
Hold this!

233
00:13:45,820 --> 00:13:46,560
Opal!

234
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:47,720
Let's go!

235
00:13:48,993 --> 00:13:50,833
Wait!

236
00:13:55,580 --> 00:13:56,620
Come on!

237
00:13:57,100 --> 00:13:58,100
Quick, run!

238
00:13:58,630 --> 00:13:59,680
She getting away!

239
00:14:03,113 --> 00:14:04,573
Help!

240
00:14:06,410 --> 00:14:08,360
Who ordered those biscuits made?!

241
00:14:08,865 --> 00:14:10,140
Those poisoned biscuits!

242
00:14:10,760 --> 00:14:11,346
Speak!

243
00:14:12,587 --> 00:14:13,553
Alright, so you won't talk.

244
00:14:13,691 --> 00:14:14,691
Fine, you don't have to!

245
00:14:14,730 --> 00:14:16,100
I'll take those biscuits!

246
00:14:16,240 --> 00:14:16,753
Out of my way!

247
00:14:17,750 --> 00:14:19,020
I'm saved!

248
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:24,480
Mr. Cookie!

249
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:26,233
Please give me those biscuits!

250
00:14:26,265 --> 00:14:27,720
Oh, Your Highness!

251
00:14:27,810 --> 00:14:28,500
N-No, I can't!

252
00:14:28,633 --> 00:14:31,380
These biscuits are for the person who ordered them!

253
00:14:31,545 --> 00:14:33,020
I'm supposed to get them!

254
00:14:33,380 --> 00:14:33,999
Please!

255
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:35,486
No, absolutely not!

256
00:14:35,590 --> 00:14:37,333
I can't hand these over!

257
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:41,400
What's wrong?

258
00:14:42,729 --> 00:14:44,620
Lord Nylon, it failed.

259
00:14:44,650 --> 00:14:45,513
It failed?

260
00:14:45,610 --> 00:14:47,500
Weren't the poisoned biscuits ready?

261
00:14:48,180 --> 00:14:48,540
What?

262
00:14:48,735 --> 00:14:50,193
Prince Sapphire showed up?

263
00:14:50,646 --> 00:14:51,120
Damn it!

264
00:14:51,580 --> 00:14:52,580
All right!

265
00:14:58,740 --> 00:14:59,740
May I help you?

266
00:15:00,579 --> 00:15:01,880
I'll handle Sapphire.

267
00:15:02,089 --> 00:15:04,780
In the meantime, go back and get the biscuits!

268
00:15:06,649 --> 00:15:07,360
You guys!

269
00:15:07,390 --> 00:15:09,240
Take care of Sapphire!

270
00:15:30,620 --> 00:15:31,040
Go!

271
00:15:31,269 --> 00:15:32,200
Good grief!

272
00:15:32,580 --> 00:15:33,933
Looks cool, doesn't it?

273
00:15:38,139 --> 00:15:39,139
Hello?

274
00:15:40,769 --> 00:15:42,020
Pardon me.

275
00:15:56,069 --> 00:15:56,960
You again!

276
00:15:56,980 --> 00:15:57,980
Villains!

277
00:16:01,140 --> 00:16:02,140
Got 'em!

278
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:03,620
Good work!

279
00:16:03,700 --> 00:16:04,720
I leave the rest to you!

280
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:13,800
Don't shoot!

281
00:16:13,820 --> 00:16:15,186
I'm Cookie!

282
00:16:16,820 --> 00:16:17,920
No, don't shoot!

283
00:16:17,975 --> 00:16:19,333
Why are you shooting?!

284
00:16:20,594 --> 00:16:24,020
We can't have you blabbing about making poisoned biscuits.

285
00:16:24,420 --> 00:16:25,386
So you'll have to die!

286
00:16:28,053 --> 00:16:28,695
Damn it!

287
00:16:28,720 --> 00:16:29,786
So that's it!

288
00:16:29,980 --> 00:16:31,413
I was tricked!

289
00:16:31,510 --> 00:16:34,666
Your Highness, I didn't know that medicine was poison.

290
00:16:34,700 --> 00:16:38,420
That's why I did as they said and made poisoned treats.

291
00:16:38,595 --> 00:16:41,046
Do you know who they're going to feed those poisoned biscuits to?

292
00:16:41,140 --> 00:16:41,940
Yes, I do.

293
00:16:42,060 --> 00:16:43,673
To everyone in the castle.

294
00:16:43,830 --> 00:16:47,439
The King, the Queen, the Prince, and... oh no!

295
00:16:47,610 --> 00:16:49,425
I forgot something terrible!

296
00:16:49,450 --> 00:16:52,106
Those biscuits were meant to be today's snack!

297
00:16:54,761 --> 00:16:55,860
Today's snack?

298
00:16:56,320 --> 00:16:57,105
Oh no!

299
00:16:57,130 --> 00:16:58,680
It's almost snack time!

300
00:16:58,820 --> 00:16:58,980
Ah!

301
00:16:59,265 --> 00:17:00,680
There's still one left over there!

302
00:17:00,900 --> 00:17:01,566
That's it!

303
00:17:04,239 --> 00:17:08,500
If we make them eat this biscuit, they'll obey us just like the Queen Mother!

304
00:17:08,900 --> 00:17:09,900
All right!

305
00:17:18,540 --> 00:17:19,700
Take this!

306
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:25,560
Ouch!

307
00:17:30,589 --> 00:17:32,620
Listen up, whoever ate the biscuit!

308
00:17:33,279 --> 00:17:35,126
You don't need to capture me anymore!

309
00:17:35,660 --> 00:17:36,740
Yes, sir!

310
00:17:37,679 --> 00:17:40,700
See? The potion in the biscuit works!

311
00:17:45,599 --> 00:17:47,820
Your Highness, we won't stand in your way anymore!

312
00:17:48,144 --> 00:17:50,980
Now, tell me who ordered you to defeat me!

313
00:17:51,966 --> 00:17:53,800
I don't know their name.

314
00:17:54,006 --> 00:17:56,020
I was only asked by the soldiers...

315
00:17:57,029 --> 00:17:58,706
Don't the others know?

316
00:18:00,294 --> 00:18:02,300
Your Grace, quickly, to the castle!

317
00:18:02,740 --> 00:18:03,740
Oh, right!

318
00:18:03,929 --> 00:18:05,606
Now, all of you, go home!

319
00:18:05,724 --> 00:18:07,493
Never come to this forest again!

320
00:18:20,569 --> 00:18:22,600
Nylon, do they taste good?!

321
00:18:22,854 --> 00:18:24,246
Of course they do!

322
00:18:24,714 --> 00:18:27,760
I had Silverland's finest baker make them!

323
00:18:27,959 --> 00:18:30,567
All right, give this to the castle cook at once...

324
00:18:30,591 --> 00:18:33,460
...and make everyone who sides with Sapphire eat it!

325
00:18:33,461 --> 00:18:34,207
Yes, sir!

326
00:18:34,489 --> 00:18:37,560
And did you get rid of the person who made the biscuits?

327
00:18:38,089 --> 00:18:40,511
They're taking care of them along with Sapphire right now.

328
00:18:40,535 --> 00:18:42,000
What, Sapphire too?!

329
00:18:42,258 --> 00:18:45,306
Are you sure about this? Sapphire is a skilled fighter!

330
00:18:46,649 --> 00:18:51,580
I'm certain it'll be fine, but... let's take one more precaution.

331
00:18:53,359 --> 00:18:55,080
Tank squad, tank squad, come in!

332
00:18:55,374 --> 00:18:57,260
This is a secret order from Lord Duralumin!

333
00:19:09,619 --> 00:19:13,700
This potion made that violent beast docile in an instant...

334
00:19:13,849 --> 00:19:17,565
<i>If Father and Mother eat it, they'll be at Lord Duralumin's mercy...</i>

335
00:19:17,589 --> 00:19:19,165
<i>Then... </i>

336
00:19:19,189 --> 00:19:21,420
Your Majesty, it's time for your snack.

337
00:19:22,677 --> 00:19:24,240
Put it on that table over there.

338
00:19:24,959 --> 00:19:26,340
Could you go call everyone else?

339
00:19:26,874 --> 00:19:27,960
We can eat together.

340
00:19:28,366 --> 00:19:29,366
Yes.

341
00:19:56,340 --> 00:19:57,340
It's a tank!

342
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:03,120
Hurry!

343
00:20:10,829 --> 00:20:12,193
Here goes!

344
00:20:27,600 --> 00:20:28,600
Stop!

345
00:20:28,829 --> 00:20:29,900
Stop, or I'll cut you down!

346
00:20:35,248 --> 00:20:36,846
Who ordered you to attack me?

347
00:20:37,304 --> 00:20:39,385
I was just following the captain's orders...

348
00:20:40,142 --> 00:20:41,021
Liar!

349
00:20:41,239 --> 00:20:42,880
Duralumin or Nylon gave the order, didn't they?

350
00:20:43,394 --> 00:20:44,900
I don't know!

351
00:20:45,020 --> 00:20:45,460
Opal!

352
00:20:45,739 --> 00:20:47,160
Just dump them somewhere!

353
00:20:49,389 --> 00:20:50,800
You guys walk back!

354
00:20:51,386 --> 00:20:52,046
Yes.

355
00:20:54,300 --> 00:20:54,940
Are they still not here?

356
00:20:55,320 --> 00:20:57,900
They'll be right here. Please, go ahead and eat.

357
00:20:58,249 --> 00:20:59,820
No, no, let's eat together.

358
00:21:00,139 --> 00:21:02,060
These biscuits look delicious.

359
00:21:06,920 --> 00:21:09,106
Sorry we're late, Your Majesty.

360
00:21:09,560 --> 00:21:10,280
You kept me waiting.

361
00:21:10,534 --> 00:21:12,060
You're always late.

362
00:21:22,419 --> 00:21:23,820
Prince Sapphire has returned!

363
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:25,293
Open the gate!

364
00:21:29,889 --> 00:21:30,889
Open the gate!

365
00:21:30,965 --> 00:21:31,965
Hurry up and open it!

366
00:21:32,160 --> 00:21:33,160
What are you doing?!

367
00:21:33,584 --> 00:21:35,500
My, these biscuits look delicious.

368
00:21:37,719 --> 00:21:40,906
If only Sapphire could bake biscuits like these...

369
00:21:41,004 --> 00:21:43,659
I'm sure Lady Sapphire will learn how to someday.

370
00:22:14,893 --> 00:22:15,673
Sapphire!

371
00:22:15,755 --> 00:22:16,840
What on earth happened?!

372
00:22:17,029 --> 00:22:18,199
Mother, Father.

373
00:22:18,679 --> 00:22:21,500
Next time, I'll bake delicious biscuits for you!

374
00:22:21,934 --> 00:22:23,159
Oh, my...

375
00:22:23,859 --> 00:22:25,380
What happened, Sapphire?

376
00:22:25,754 --> 00:22:27,033
Tell me about it.

377
00:22:27,800 --> 00:22:28,233
Okay.

378
00:22:28,719 --> 00:22:32,920
But without proof, we don't know who had those biscuits made.

379
00:22:35,114 --> 00:22:36,386
What is it?!

380
00:22:36,544 --> 00:22:40,873
Sapphire used the biscuits to turn our men to her side!

381
00:22:41,834 --> 00:22:43,080
You fools!

382
00:22:51,066 --> 00:22:52,066
Oh, my...

383
00:22:54,549 --> 00:22:57,700
They're a bit burnt, but Mr. Cookie taught me.

384
00:22:57,810 --> 00:22:58,579
They're tasty! Huh?

385
00:22:59,834 --> 00:23:01,620
Hey, these are actually pretty good.

386
00:23:02,200 --> 00:23:02,733
They really are.

387
00:23:02,914 --> 00:23:04,280
Pretty good for your first try.

388
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:05,635
Of course they are!

389
00:23:05,660 --> 00:23:06,846
Because I made them!

390
00:23:08,490 --> 00:23:09,160
So bitter!

391
00:23:09,475 --> 00:23:10,294
Darn it!

392
00:23:11,489 --> 00:23:15,740
Sapphire, you can do things girls do just fine.

393
00:23:16,284 --> 00:23:19,120
With some effort, you could even bake the world's best cake.

394
00:23:20,700 --> 00:23:20,980
Yeah!

395
00:23:21,453 --> 00:23:23,199
I'll get better, Father. You'll see.

